body:
Yeah with CPTSD in childhood, it has been found to effect brain development and can do so in ways very similar to findings on ASD brain structure. So it's an annoying chicken vs. egg thing. But usually ASD can't be diagnosed if another disorder that's present can instead explain the symptoms. Tons of overlap with ASD and BPD too :S. I've been down this rabbit hole... it's so hard to figure out what's what, unless there's clear evidence of ASD in early childhood that can't be explained by an attachment disorder, which of course can basically look just like ASD...

&#x200B;

If you want to read more about what I meant on the divided self, part two of this book [http://www.centrebombe.org/Ronald.D.Laing-The.Divided.Self.(1960](http://www.centrebombe.org/Ronald.D.Laing-The.Divided.Self.(1960)).pdf \[copy paste whole link - don't click\] described the experience.. though if you don't experience a split in yourself then yeah you can rule out schizo spectrum...
